<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zenodorus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 20 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zenodorus was an Ituraean ruler of the 1st century BCE who leased the lands of Lysanias, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trachonitis">Trachonitis</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hauran">Auranitis</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batanaea">Batanaea</a>. Accused of tolerating brigands, he lost these territories when Augustus gave them to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-the-great">Herod the Great</a> in 23 BCE, and on his death in 20 BCE Augustus gave Herod his remaining lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banias">Paneas</a>.</p></div>
